  "id": "dyad",
  "term": "dyad",
  "definition": "A dyad is a pair of people in a relationship where each person’s traits, actions, and experiences can affect both themselves and the other person. In care settings, it often refers to a care recipient and an informal carer who rely on and influence one another.",
